ary_8", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le12ob10re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Making Requests"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use a variety of phrases to make requests."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Do you think you could introduce me to Aunt Nelly sometime?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Is there any chance you could wear that blue shirt?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use modals to make requests.</p> For example:</br> Could you..?</br> Can you..?</br> Would you mind if\u2026?</p> You can also use other phrases with these modals to make requests.</p> For example:</p> Do you think you could..?</br> Is there any chance you can\u2026?"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "housework"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "work done at home like laundry, cleaning etc."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I usually help with the housework."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le12ob10aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about daily routines."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "polo shirt"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a collared T-shirt"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Could you wear that blue polo shirt?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le12ob10aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to spend "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to use"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I spend a lot of time thinking about you."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le12ob10aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to help out"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to help someone do something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I like to help out with the housework."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le12ob10aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "rest "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the remaining amount"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: What about the rest of the day?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le12ob10aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "nervous"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "anxious; worried"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I sometimes get nervous when I meet my girlfriend's family."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le12ob10aud06"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ask your partner about what they do to help out around the house."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a list of the things they do. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a list of the things you do. How do the lists compare?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a paragraph comparing you and your partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read the paragraph to another person."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I ask my partner questions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make a list and write a paragraph."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use words that talk about frequency."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read the paragraph to another person."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "conten